  "solution": {
    "text": "Let,&nbsp;<math><mi>M</mi><mo>→</mo></math>Mathematics, <math><mi>P</mi><mo>→</mo></math>Physics, <math><mi>C</mi><mo>→</mo></math>Chemistry<br />Given that total students <math><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>M</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>120</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>P</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>C</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>,</mo></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>43</mn></math><br /><math><mi>n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mn>8</mn></math><br />Required number of students taking exactly one subject is<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>M</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>P</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>C</mi></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>∩</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>∩</mo><m